#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:4
msgid "Fast and slow: the two categories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:6
msgid "Everything this page describes rests on one split, so it comes first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:9
msgid "Why a gate that costs a minute gates nothing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:11
msgid ""
"The more often the tests, the linters and the coverage run, the more "
"solid the tree. That is the entire argument for checking at every commit "
"rather than at every release, and it is a good one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:14
msgid ""
"It is also an argument that turns on itself the moment the gate costs "
"real time. A person who waits a minute to commit commits less often. "
"Fewer, larger commits are harder to review and harder to bisect; then "
"somebody discovers ``--no-verify``; then the gate is a decoration. **A "
"cheap check that runs a hundred times a week is worth more than a "
"thorough one that runs on Fridays** — not because thoroughness does not "
"matter, but because a check that is skipped has no value at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:20
msgid ""
"So the checks are sorted by **cost, not by importance**. Nothing here is "
"optional; the question is only when it is paid for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:24
msgid "What makes something slow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:26
msgid ""
"Two different expenses, and this workspace treats them as one category "
"because the gate has to make the same decision about both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:34
msgid "It costs time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:35
msgid "It needs the network"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:36
msgid "Why it is out"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:37
msgid "minutes, or seconds multiplied by every commit of a working day"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:38
msgid ""
"it depends on a host nobody here controls, so it can fail for a reason "
"that has nothing to do with the commit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:40
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:41
msgid ""
"the instrumented Rust coverage build, the crate's integration tests and "
"doctests, the process-per-test half of the tooling suite, a formats "
"repository's whole-document runs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:43
msgid "resolving methodology pages, looking a granter's key up on a key server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:44
msgid "Told apart by"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:45
msgid "``cost`` in the registry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:46
msgid "``online`` beside it, which only changes the *message*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:48
msgid ""
"They are kept apart in the tables so that a message can say *which* it is"
" — \"run it\" and \"check your network\" are different things to tell "
"somebody — and gated alike, because \"can this be paid for at every "
"commit\" has the same answer for both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:52
msgid ""
"A check is **fast** when it runs locally, needs no network, no second "
"toolchain and no instrumented rebuild, and costs a second or so. "
"Everything else is slow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:56
msgid "What the split is *not*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:58
msgid ""
"It is not \"the checks\" and \"the optional checks\". It is **what this "
"commit was checked against** and **what it was not** — and the second "
"half is written down, at every commit, in the same table as the first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:62
msgid ""
"That is what the rest of this page is about: every suite records its "
"outcome *and the commit it ran at*, every slow metric records the commit "
"it was measured at, and ``ci-check`` — which measures nothing and costs a"
" fifth of a second — prints a suite nobody ran here as ``NOT RUN`` and a "
"figure from an earlier commit as ``STALE``. Neither can be read as a "
"pass, for the same reason ``unmeasured`` cannot: **something nobody "
"established is not something that holds.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/fast-and-slow.rst:68
msgid ""
"On ``dev`` that is a notification and the work continues. On ``prod`` "
"every one of them refuses, and the branch's gate is the slow one, so that"
" nothing about a production commit is unknown."
msgstr ""

